<article class="env-lemma" id="00KI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00KI">Lemma <span data-tag="00KI">10.60.6</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring. Then $\dim (R) = 0 \Leftrightarrow d(R) = 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is because $d(R) = 0$ if and only if $R$ has finite length as an $R$-module. See Lemma <a href="/tag/00JB" data-tag="00JB">10.53.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>